WEBVTT

00:03:32.090 --> 00:03:35.250
Who am I? You sure you want to know?

00:03:35.450 --> 00:03:38.710
The story of my life
is not for the faint of heart.

00:03:38.870 --> 00:03:41.500
If somebody said
it was a happy little tale...

00:03:41.710 --> 00:03:46.160
... if somebody told you I was just an
average guy, not a care in the world...

00:03:46.330 --> 00:03:48.120
... somebody lied.

00:03:49.000 --> 00:03:52.580
But let me assure you, this,
like any story worth telling...

00:03:52.740 --> 00:03:54.160
... is all about a girl.

00:03:55.040 --> 00:03:59.500
That girl. The girl next door.
Mary Jane Watson.

00:03:59.670 --> 00:04:02.740
The woman I've loved
since before I liked girls.

00:04:02.910 --> 00:04:05.580
I'd like to tell you that's me
next to her.

00:04:05.750 --> 00:04:07.750
Aw, heck, I'd even take him.

00:04:09.170 --> 00:04:11.660
Hey! Stop the bus!

00:04:12.660 --> 00:04:13.830
That's me.

00:04:14.040 --> 00:04:15.910
Tell him to stop! Please!

00:04:16.120 --> 00:04:17.330
Stop!

00:04:17.540 --> 00:04:19.740
Hey! Stop the bus!

00:04:19.910 --> 00:04:22.990
Stop! He's been chasing us
since Woodhaven.

00:04:23.160 --> 00:04:24.410
Catch a cab, Parker!

00:04:28.860 --> 00:04:31.660
Thank you. I'm sorry I'm late.

00:04:37.080 --> 00:04:38.360
What a geek!

00:04:39.030 --> 00:04:43.240
- Don't even think about it.
- You're so lame, Parker.

00:04:43.410 --> 00:04:45.000
Would you date him?

00:05:02.870 --> 00:05:05.080
Midtown High seniors.

00:05:05.250 --> 00:05:08.950
No wandering. Proceed direct...
Knock it off.

00:05:09.240 --> 00:05:12.700
Remember, it is a privilege
to be here.

00:05:13.080 --> 00:05:16.320
We're guests of Columbia University's
Science Department.

00:05:16.530 --> 00:05:18.740
So behave accordingly.

00:05:18.910 --> 00:05:21.950
Let's not have a repeat
of our trip to the planetarium.

00:05:22.160 --> 00:05:23.790
Come on, stay together.

00:05:23.940 --> 00:05:26.860
Proceed up the steps
and into the building.

00:05:28.030 --> 00:05:31.070
- Where were you?
- Checking out the library.

00:05:31.240 --> 00:05:33.780
- Looking at the books.
- Yeah, right.

00:05:35.530 --> 00:05:39.360
- Can we drive around the corner?
- Why?

00:05:39.570 --> 00:05:41.370
The entrance is right there.

00:05:41.530 --> 00:05:45.240
Dad, this is public school.
I can't show up in a Rolls.

00:05:45.440 --> 00:05:47.780
I should trade my car for a Jetta...

00:05:47.950 --> 00:05:50.740
...because you flunked out
of private school?

00:05:51.030 --> 00:05:54.070
- It wasn't for me.
- Of course it was.

00:05:54.730 --> 00:05:59.070
- Don't ever be ashamed of who you are.
- I'm not ashamed of who I am.

00:05:59.280 --> 00:06:00.570
It's just...

00:06:00.740 --> 00:06:02.190
Just what, Harry?

00:06:02.400 --> 00:06:03.900
Forget it.

00:06:06.900 --> 00:06:08.240
Pete!

00:06:08.660 --> 00:06:11.150
- Hi, Harry.
- Hey, man. What's up?

00:06:12.020 --> 00:06:14.230
- Won't you be needing this?
- Thanks.

00:06:15.190 --> 00:06:19.160
- This is my father, Norman Osborn.
- I've heard so much about you.

00:06:19.360 --> 00:06:22.820
- It's an honor, sir.
- Harry says you're a science whiz.

00:06:23.070 --> 00:06:25.900
I'm something of a scientist myself.

00:06:26.070 --> 00:06:29.230
I read your research
on nanotechnology. Brilliant.

00:06:29.400 --> 00:06:32.440
- You understood it?
- Yes, I wrote a paper on it.

00:06:32.650 --> 00:06:35.940
Impressive.
Your parents must be very proud.

00:06:36.110 --> 00:06:40.650
- I live with my aunt and uncle.
- Hey, you two! Let's move!

00:06:40.810 --> 00:06:44.480
- Nice to meet you.
- Hope to see you again.

00:06:46.820 --> 00:06:50.310
- He doesn't seem so bad.
- Not if you're a genius.

00:06:50.480 --> 00:06:52.440
I think he wants to adopt you.

00:06:52.610 --> 00:06:53.230
There are over 32,000 known species
of spider in the world.

00:06:53.230 --> 00:06:57.310
There are over 32,000 known species
of spider in the world.

00:06:57.520 --> 00:07:01.310
They're in the order Araneae,
divided into three suborders.

00:07:01.520 --> 00:07:02.610
That's amazing!

00:07:02.770 --> 00:07:06.690
This is the most advanced electron
microscope on the East Coast.

00:07:07.020 --> 00:07:09.060
It's unreal.

00:07:09.230 --> 00:07:12.020
Arachnids from all three
groups possess...

00:07:12.230 --> 00:07:15.730
...varying strengths
to help them search for food.

00:07:15.930 --> 00:07:20.150
For example, the Delena spider,
family Sparassidae...

00:07:20.310 --> 00:07:24.480
...has the ability to jump
to catch its prey.

00:07:24.640 --> 00:07:26.390
For the school paper?

00:07:30.900 --> 00:07:35.890
Next, we have the net web spider,
family Filistatidae...

00:07:36.100 --> 00:07:37.980
...genus Kukulcania.

00:07:38.230 --> 00:07:42.570
Spins a funnel- shaped web whose
strands have a tensile strength...

00:07:42.770 --> 00:07:48.020
...proportionately equal to
the high-tension wires used in bridges.

00:07:48.480 --> 00:07:50.150
- Leave him alone.
- Or what?

00:07:50.310 --> 00:07:53.310
Or his father will fire your father.

00:07:53.720 --> 00:07:56.060
What's Daddy gonna do? Sue me?

00:07:56.230 --> 00:07:58.730
What is going on?

00:07:58.900 --> 00:08:01.970
The next person who talks
will fail this course.

00:08:02.180 --> 00:08:04.180
- This spider...
- Let's go.

00:08:04.350 --> 00:08:08.520
...hunts using reflexes with
nerve- conduction velocity so fast...

00:08:08.730 --> 00:08:12.220
...that some researchers believe
it borders on precognition.

00:08:12.390 --> 00:08:14.560
- An early awareness of danger.
- Jerks.

00:08:14.770 --> 00:08:16.520
A spider- sense.

00:08:17.140 --> 00:08:18.810
Hey, look at that spider.

00:08:18.980 --> 00:08:23.390
Some spiders change colors
to blend into their environment.

00:08:23.640 --> 00:08:25.560
It's a defense mechanism.

00:08:25.730 --> 00:08:29.020
Peter, what makes you think
I'd want to know that?

00:08:29.190 --> 00:08:30.390
Who wouldn't?

00:08:30.550 --> 00:08:34.390
Over five painstaking years,
Columbia's research facility...

00:08:34.560 --> 00:08:38.930
- You gonna talk to her now?
- Oh, no. Come on. You talk to her.

00:08:39.140 --> 00:08:43.890
With these DNA blueprints, we have
begun what was once thought impossible.

00:08:44.100 --> 00:08:47.770
- Disgusting.
- Yeah, hateful little things.

00:08:47.980 --> 00:08:49.340
I love them!

00:08:49.890 --> 00:08:51.560
Yeah, me too.

00:08:52.510 --> 00:08:56.390
You know, spiders can change
their color...

00:08:56.560 --> 00:09:00.390
...to blend into their environment.
- Really?

00:09:00.550 --> 00:09:04.680
- Yeah, it's a defense mechanism.
- Cool.

00:09:04.890 --> 00:09:08.260
- Transfer RNA
to encode an entirely new genome...

00:09:08.430 --> 00:09:11.560
...combining the genetic
information from all three...

00:09:11.720 --> 00:09:16.380
...into these 15 genetically
designed super- spiders.

00:09:16.550 --> 00:09:18.050
There's 14.

00:09:18.510 --> 00:09:19.890
I beg your pardon?

00:09:20.050 --> 00:09:22.600
- One's missing.
- Yeah.

00:09:25.510 --> 00:09:28.140
I guess the researchers
are working on that one.

00:09:28.640 --> 00:09:33.350
Do you know that this is the largest
electron microscope on the East Coast?

00:09:33.520 --> 00:09:37.590
You were talking throughout
that woman's entire presentation.

00:09:37.760 --> 00:09:39.510
Let's talk about listening.

00:09:43.600 --> 00:09:46.340
I don't know what it's like
at those fancy private schools...

00:09:46.340 --> 00:09:47.680
I don't know what it's like
at those fancy private schools...

00:09:47.880 --> 00:09:49.760
...but at Midtown High...

00:09:58.220 --> 00:10:01.970
Could I take your picture?
I need one with a student in it.

00:10:02.140 --> 00:10:03.590
- Sure.
- Great.

00:10:03.800 --> 00:10:06.090
Where do you want me?
Over here?

00:10:06.300 --> 00:10:07.630
Yeah, that's great.

00:10:08.050 --> 00:10:09.720
Don't make me look ugly.

00:10:10.100 --> 00:10:11.920
That's impossible.

00:10:19.180 --> 00:10:20.430
Perfect.

00:10:28.180 --> 00:10:29.720
- Is that good?
- Great.

00:10:35.260 --> 00:10:36.630
That's great.

00:10:42.210 --> 00:10:44.210
M.J., let's go!

00:10:45.760 --> 00:10:48.340
Wait. Thanks!

00:11:01.800 --> 00:11:04.550
Parker, let's do it.

00:11:21.250 --> 00:11:24.720
We've solved the horizon glide
and the balance issues.

00:11:24.880 --> 00:11:27.420
I've already seen the glider.

00:11:27.830 --> 00:11:29.880
That's not what I'm here for.

00:11:30.090 --> 00:11:32.750
General Slocum, good to see you again.

00:11:33.590 --> 00:11:35.750
Mr. Balkan, Mr. Fargas.

00:11:36.000 --> 00:11:37.830
- Norman.
- Mr. Osborn.

00:11:38.000 --> 00:11:41.550
Always a pleasure to have
our board of directors visit.

00:11:41.750 --> 00:11:45.160
I want the report on human
performance enhancers.

00:11:45.330 --> 00:11:49.840
We tried vapor inhalation with rats.
Their strength increased by 800%.

00:11:50.000 --> 00:11:51.880
- Excellent.
- Any side effects?

00:11:52.050 --> 00:11:53.130
Once.

00:11:53.300 --> 00:11:55.960
All the tests since
have been successful.

00:11:56.120 --> 00:11:59.880
In the trial that went wrong,
what were the side effects?

00:12:00.040 --> 00:12:02.380
Violence, aggression...

00:12:03.050 --> 00:12:04.290
...and insanity.

00:12:04.450 --> 00:12:07.210
- What do you recommend?
- That was only one test.

00:12:07.460 --> 00:12:11.300
Except for Dr. Stromm,
our staff certifies the product...

00:12:11.460 --> 00:12:14.370
...ready for human testing.
- Dr. Stromm?

00:12:15.710 --> 00:12:19.380
We need to take the whole line
back to formula.

00:12:20.630 --> 00:12:23.040
- Back to formula?
- Dr. Osborn.

00:12:24.200 --> 00:12:26.040
I'll be frank with you.

00:12:26.290 --> 00:12:31.120
I never supported your program. We
have my predecessor to thank for that.

00:12:31.290 --> 00:12:34.040
The general has approved
Quest Aerospace...

00:12:34.200 --> 00:12:37.120
...to build a prototype
of their exoskeleton.

00:12:37.460 --> 00:12:41.370
- They test in two weeks.
- And if your performance enhancers...

00:12:41.540 --> 00:12:45.620
...have not had a successful
human trial by that date...

00:12:45.870 --> 00:12:50.240
...l'm gonna pull your funding.
I'm going to give it to them.

00:12:52.040 --> 00:12:53.700
Gentlemen. Ladies.

00:12:58.780 --> 00:13:04.200
And the Lord said, "Let there be light."
And voilÃ ! There is light.

00:13:04.460 --> 00:13:06.540
Forty soft, glowing watts of it.

00:13:06.710 --> 00:13:11.540
Good boy. God will be thrilled.
Just don't fall on your ass.

00:13:11.870 --> 00:13:14.290
I'm already on my ass, May.

00:13:14.460 --> 00:13:18.950
When the plant's senior electrician
is laid off after 35 years...

00:13:19.120 --> 00:13:21.830
...what would you call it?
I am on my ass.

00:13:22.040 --> 00:13:24.370
Hand me that dish. The green one.

00:13:24.620 --> 00:13:27.360
The corporation is downsizing
the people...

00:13:27.820 --> 00:13:29.700
...and upsizing their profits.

00:13:29.950 --> 00:13:32.870
Oh, Ben, you'll get another job
somewhere.

00:13:33.870 --> 00:13:36.780
Well, let's look
in the paper and see.

00:13:37.910 --> 00:13:40.700
There are the want ads.
What do we got here?

00:13:40.870 --> 00:13:42.490
Computer...

00:13:42.700 --> 00:13:46.450
Computer salesman, computer engineer,
computer analyst.

00:13:46.610 --> 00:13:50.370
My Lord, even the computers
need analysts these days.

00:13:50.660 --> 00:13:55.950
I'm 68. I'm too old for computers, and
besides, I have a family to provide for.

00:13:56.160 --> 00:13:59.030
I love you. And Peter loves you.

00:13:59.280 --> 00:14:02.540
You're the most responsible man
I've ever known.

00:14:02.790 --> 00:14:07.200
We've been down-and-out before.
But somehow, we survive.

00:14:08.320 --> 00:14:12.620
Hi, sweetie. You're just...
Just in time for dinner.

00:14:12.830 --> 00:14:15.360
How you doing? How was the field trip?

00:14:15.530 --> 00:14:18.370
I don't feel well.
I'm gonna go to sleep.

00:14:18.530 --> 00:14:21.040
- You won't have a bite?
- Had a bite.

00:14:21.200 --> 00:14:23.610
Did you get some pictures, Peter?

00:14:24.450 --> 00:14:27.280
I gotta crash. Everything's fine.

00:14:28.700 --> 00:14:30.280
What's that all about?

00:14:51.530 --> 00:14:53.740
In this recombination lab...

00:14:53.900 --> 00:14:58.530
... we use synthesized transfer RNA
to encode an entirely new genome...

00:14:58.740 --> 00:15:01.780
... combining the genetic
information from all three...

00:15:01.980 --> 00:15:06.780
... into these 15 genetically
designed super-spiders.

00:15:21.230 --> 00:15:25.200
Dr. Osborn, please.
The performance enhancers aren't ready.

00:15:25.360 --> 00:15:28.690
The data just doesn't justify
this test.

00:15:28.860 --> 00:15:32.530
Now, I'm asking you for the last time.
We can't do this.

00:15:32.690 --> 00:15:34.900
Don't be a coward.

00:15:35.360 --> 00:15:37.940
Risks are part of laboratory science.

00:15:38.150 --> 00:15:41.860
Let me reschedule,
with a medical staff and a volunteer.

00:15:42.070 --> 00:15:44.530
- Just give me two weeks.
- Two weeks?

00:15:44.700 --> 00:15:49.190
In two weeks? We'll have lost the contract
to Quest and OSCORP will be dead.

00:15:49.360 --> 00:15:52.110
Sometimes you gotta
do things yourself.

00:15:52.280 --> 00:15:54.950
- Get me the Promachloraperazine.
- For what?

00:15:55.100 --> 00:15:58.860
It begins catalyzation when the vapor
hits the bloodstream.

00:16:01.780 --> 00:16:03.440
40,000 years of evolution...

00:16:03.610 --> 00:16:07.350
...and we've barely tapped
the vastness of human potential.

00:16:21.190 --> 00:16:22.530
Oh, that's cold.

00:17:20.930 --> 00:17:22.180
Norman?

00:17:26.690 --> 00:17:27.970
Norman!

00:17:38.680 --> 00:17:40.010
Oh, my God.

00:17:41.520 --> 00:17:42.930
Oh, my God!

00:17:45.600 --> 00:17:47.430
Oh, my God! Norman!

00:18:03.810 --> 00:18:05.430
Back to formula?

00:18:40.010 --> 00:18:41.520
Weird.

00:18:52.420 --> 00:18:53.800
- Peter?
- Yeah?

00:18:54.010 --> 00:18:55.760
Are you all right?

00:18:57.680 --> 00:18:59.310
I'm fine.

00:18:59.890 --> 00:19:03.260
- Any better this morning? Any change?
- Change?

00:19:04.260 --> 00:19:06.180
Yep. Big change.

00:19:06.340 --> 00:19:10.340
- Well, hurry up. You'll be late.
- Right.

00:19:28.710 --> 00:19:30.090
Okay.

00:19:34.800 --> 00:19:38.590
- Goodness me!
- Jeez. I thought you were sick.

00:19:39.130 --> 00:19:40.460
- I got better.
- See?

00:19:40.630 --> 00:19:44.010
- Bye, guys.
- Have you got your lunch money?

00:19:44.180 --> 00:19:47.840
Don't forget, we're painting
the kitchen after school.

00:19:48.000 --> 00:19:50.800
Sure, Uncle Ben.
Don't start without me.

00:19:51.010 --> 00:19:53.090
And don't start up with me.

00:19:54.680 --> 00:19:58.340
Teenagers. Raging hormones.
They never change.

00:19:59.300 --> 00:20:03.010
You're trash!
You're always gonna be trash!

00:20:03.170 --> 00:20:06.750
- I have to go to school.
- Who's stopping you?

00:20:24.130 --> 00:20:25.790
Hi, M.J.

00:20:26.670 --> 00:20:28.170
Hey, M.J.

00:20:28.420 --> 00:20:32.970
I don't know if you realize this, but
we've been neighbors since I was 6.

00:20:33.130 --> 00:20:36.460
And I was wondering
if we could get together sometime?

00:20:36.670 --> 00:20:37.960
I got the car. Hop in.

00:20:38.130 --> 00:20:41.010
Do something fun?
Or, I don't know.

00:20:41.210 --> 00:20:45.040
I thought it'd be time
to get to know each other.

00:20:45.290 --> 00:20:46.540
Or not.

00:20:52.010 --> 00:20:54.710
Sorry, Parker, the bus is full!

00:20:56.250 --> 00:20:58.790
- Stop the bus!
- Catch a cab!

00:20:59.210 --> 00:21:00.840
Tell him to stop.

00:21:01.500 --> 00:21:03.500
- Check him out!
- Dork!

00:21:25.960 --> 00:21:27.210
Dad!

00:21:27.670 --> 00:21:29.540
Dad, are you all right?

00:21:30.370 --> 00:21:31.660
Harry.

00:21:35.000 --> 00:21:37.000
What are you doing on the floor?

00:21:37.170 --> 00:21:38.500
I don't know.

00:21:39.330 --> 00:21:41.660
Have you been there all night?

00:21:43.660 --> 00:21:44.920
Last night I was...

00:21:47.250 --> 00:21:48.490
What?

00:21:49.740 --> 00:21:52.160
- I don't remember.
- Mr. Osborn?

00:21:52.370 --> 00:21:54.040
Sir, I asked her to wait.

00:21:54.210 --> 00:21:58.530
- My father's not feeling well...
- Mr. Osborn, Dr. Stromm is dead.

00:21:58.700 --> 00:21:59.740
What?

00:21:59.910 --> 00:22:03.500
They found his body in the lab.
He's been murdered, sir.

00:22:03.660 --> 00:22:07.030
- What?
- And the flight suit and the glider...

00:22:07.200 --> 00:22:09.200
- What about it?
- Stolen, sir.

00:22:34.120 --> 00:22:36.870
Wow! Great reflexes!

00:22:37.740 --> 00:22:39.910
- Thanks.
- No problem.

00:22:41.000 --> 00:22:44.910
Hey, you have blue eyes.
I didn't notice without your glasses.

00:22:45.660 --> 00:22:47.330
You just get contacts?

00:22:54.070 --> 00:22:56.240
Well, see you.

00:23:37.990 --> 00:23:41.490
- What happened?
- He's freaking weird.

00:23:41.940 --> 00:23:43.320
Did you see that?

00:23:44.910 --> 00:23:46.570
Parker?

00:24:18.400 --> 00:24:20.820
- It's a fight!
- Think you're funny?

00:24:20.990 --> 00:24:23.990
- It was an accident.
- So is my breaking your teeth.

00:24:24.200 --> 00:24:26.900
- Flash, stop.
- I don't want to fight you.

00:24:27.070 --> 00:24:30.490
- I wouldn't want to fight me neither.
- Kick his ass.

00:24:49.360 --> 00:24:50.690
Help him, Harry.

00:24:55.650 --> 00:24:57.150
How'd he do that?

00:24:58.230 --> 00:24:59.480
Which one?

00:24:59.650 --> 00:25:01.030
He's all yours, man.

00:25:16.520 --> 00:25:18.230
Flash, get up!

00:25:19.860 --> 00:25:22.980
Jesus, Parker, you are a freak.

00:25:24.900 --> 00:25:26.400
That was amazing.

00:25:27.320 --> 00:25:29.320
I'm out of here. Come on.

00:27:14.390 --> 00:27:15.430
Go, web!

00:27:17.010 --> 00:27:18.640
Fly.

00:27:20.230 --> 00:27:22.300
Up, up and away, web.

00:27:23.890 --> 00:27:25.300
Shazam!

00:27:25.890 --> 00:27:27.140
Go! Go!

00:27:27.390 --> 00:27:29.140
Go, web, go!

00:28:02.220 --> 00:28:03.970
Tallyho.

00:28:47.840 --> 00:28:50.420
- Is she back with the beer yet?
- What?

00:28:50.630 --> 00:28:51.880
Bring me some beer.

00:28:52.090 --> 00:28:54.640
- Get up off your ass.
- I paid for beer...

00:28:54.790 --> 00:28:56.290
- Stop yelling.
- Stop it!

00:28:56.460 --> 00:28:58.800
You're as stupid as your mother.

00:29:00.720 --> 00:29:03.260
Where's she going?
Where you going?

00:29:04.330 --> 00:29:07.670
The dishes aren't done.
Somebody's gotta do dishes.

00:29:07.880 --> 00:29:11.170
- Why don't you do them?
- Get in here and do the dishes.

00:29:11.380 --> 00:29:15.500
- You do them. They're yours, anyway.
- I'm going out!

00:29:15.710 --> 00:29:18.210
- Were you listening to that?
- No.

00:29:18.550 --> 00:29:21.800
Well, I heard, but I was
just taking out the trash.

00:29:21.970 --> 00:29:24.710
I guess you can always hear us.

00:29:24.880 --> 00:29:27.170
Everybody shouts.

00:29:27.630 --> 00:29:29.760
Your aunt and uncle don't.

00:29:29.920 --> 00:29:32.460
Oh, they can scream
pretty good sometimes.

00:29:33.880 --> 00:29:38.090
Listen, M.J., about today
at school with Flash...

00:29:38.340 --> 00:29:39.960
You really freaked us out.

00:29:40.170 --> 00:29:42.420
I'm sorry. Is he okay?

00:29:42.710 --> 00:29:46.670
He's just happy you didn't give him
a black eye for graduation.

00:29:49.760 --> 00:29:52.960
So where are you going
after you graduate?

00:29:57.710 --> 00:30:00.000
I wanna move into the city.

00:30:00.910 --> 00:30:05.710
And hopefully, get a job
as a photographer.

00:30:05.880 --> 00:30:08.710
Work my way through college.

00:30:09.700 --> 00:30:11.040
What about you?

00:30:11.210 --> 00:30:13.210
Headed for the city too.

00:30:13.920 --> 00:30:16.170
Can't wait to get out of here.

00:30:17.340 --> 00:30:18.830
I wanna...

00:30:20.080 --> 00:30:21.580
What?

00:30:24.420 --> 00:30:26.670
No, come on. Try me.

00:30:27.590 --> 00:30:29.080
I wanna...

00:30:30.210 --> 00:30:31.540
...act...

00:30:32.710 --> 00:30:34.210
...on-stage.

00:30:34.790 --> 00:30:36.630
Really?

00:30:36.990 --> 00:30:39.160
Oh, that's perfect.

00:30:39.450 --> 00:30:42.000
You were awesome
in all the school plays.

00:30:42.330 --> 00:30:44.170
- Really?
- Yeah.

00:30:44.790 --> 00:30:47.790
I cried like a baby
when you played Cinderella.

00:30:48.290 --> 00:30:50.500
Peter, that was first grade.

00:30:51.000 --> 00:30:52.500
Well...

00:30:53.040 --> 00:30:54.540
...even so.

00:30:55.530 --> 00:30:57.450
Sometimes...

00:30:58.290 --> 00:30:59.960
...you know people.

00:31:01.120 --> 00:31:04.710
You can just see what's coming.

00:31:07.790 --> 00:31:10.540
What do you see coming for you?

00:31:13.120 --> 00:31:14.780
I don't know.

00:31:17.120 --> 00:31:21.790
Whatever it is, it's something
I never felt before.

00:31:25.370 --> 00:31:28.290
And what for me?

00:31:28.450 --> 00:31:29.790
For you?

00:31:31.210 --> 00:31:33.950
You're gonna light up Broadway.

00:31:35.450 --> 00:31:36.790
You know...

00:31:41.160 --> 00:31:43.780
...you're taller than you look.

00:31:43.950 --> 00:31:45.490
I hunch.

00:31:47.740 --> 00:31:49.250
Don't.

00:31:52.780 --> 00:31:56.330
Hey, M.J.! Come take a ride
in my new birthday present.

00:31:57.410 --> 00:31:58.700
Come on.

00:31:59.790 --> 00:32:01.110
I gotta go.

00:32:01.950 --> 00:32:03.110
Bye.

00:32:03.780 --> 00:32:06.450
- Oh, my God, it's gorgeous!
- Yeah, right.

00:32:06.620 --> 00:32:08.620
- Look at it!
- Hop in.

00:32:08.790 --> 00:32:11.030
Oh, my God. What a cool car!

00:32:11.280 --> 00:32:12.860
Pretty tight, huh?

00:32:13.280 --> 00:32:17.620
Wait till you hear the sound system.
Hey, don't scratch the leather.

00:32:19.360 --> 00:32:20.610
Cool car.

00:33:53.230 --> 00:33:55.270
What's going on in there?

00:33:55.480 --> 00:33:58.110
I'm exercising.
I'm not dressed, Aunt May.

00:33:58.280 --> 00:34:01.940
Well, you're acting
so strangely, Peter.

00:34:02.230 --> 00:34:04.310
Okay. Thanks.

00:34:35.110 --> 00:34:38.430
Something's wrong.
Maybe he's too embarrassed to tell me.

00:34:38.600 --> 00:34:41.270
Maybe I'm too embarrassed to ask him.

00:34:42.060 --> 00:34:44.110
I just don't know anymore.

00:34:44.520 --> 00:34:47.070
I'm going to the library.
See you later.

00:34:47.280 --> 00:34:50.640
- Wait. I'll drive you there.
- I'll take the train.

00:34:50.810 --> 00:34:54.060
No, I need the exercise.
Go on. Go, go.

00:35:05.110 --> 00:35:08.560
- Thanks for the ride, Uncle Ben.
- Wait. We need to talk.

00:35:08.730 --> 00:35:13.110
- We can talk later.
- Well, we can talk now. If you let me.

00:35:13.980 --> 00:35:16.220
What do we have to talk about?
Why now?

00:35:16.390 --> 00:35:20.440
We haven't talked for so long.
May and I don't know who you are.

00:35:20.600 --> 00:35:25.600
You shirk your chores. You have all
those weird experiments in your room.

00:35:25.760 --> 00:35:29.890
- You start fights at school.
- I told you I didn't start that fight.

00:35:30.100 --> 00:35:33.060
- You sure finished it.
- Was I supposed to run away?

00:35:33.270 --> 00:35:36.270
No, you're not supposed
to run away, but...

00:35:36.430 --> 00:35:40.980
You're changing. I went through
exactly the same thing at your age.

00:35:41.190 --> 00:35:43.190
No. Not exactly.

00:35:44.550 --> 00:35:47.270
These are the years
when a man changes...

00:35:47.430 --> 00:35:51.440
...into the man he's gonna become
the rest of his life.

00:35:51.600 --> 00:35:54.680
Just be careful who you change into.

00:35:56.220 --> 00:36:00.730
This guy, Flash Thompson,
he probably deserved what happened.

00:36:01.270 --> 00:36:03.970
But just because you can
beat him up...

00:36:04.430 --> 00:36:06.680
...doesn't give you the right to.

00:36:07.350 --> 00:36:12.590
Remember, with great power
comes great responsibility.

00:36:13.180 --> 00:36:18.180
Are you afraid I'll become a criminal?
Quit worrying about me, okay?

00:36:18.350 --> 00:36:21.760
Something's different.
I'll figure it out. Stop lecturing.

00:36:22.050 --> 00:36:26.270
I don't mean to lecture or preach.
And I know I'm not your father.

00:36:26.430 --> 00:36:29.270
Then stop pretending to be!

00:36:33.350 --> 00:36:34.600
Right.

00:36:37.560 --> 00:36:39.510
I'll pick you up here at 10.

00:37:10.720 --> 00:37:11.220
Bone Saw! Bone Saw! Bone Saw!

00:37:11.220 --> 00:37:13.390
Bone Saw! Bone Saw! Bone Saw!

00:37:13.390 --> 00:37:16.550
Bone Saw! Bone Saw! Bone Saw!

00:37:21.260 --> 00:37:25.300
- One, two, three. That's it!
- Who's the man?

00:37:29.420 --> 00:37:31.640
Ladies and gentlemen...

00:37:31.800 --> 00:37:36.340
...give it up for Bone Saw McGraw.

00:37:39.420 --> 00:37:43.100
For $3000...

00:37:43.260 --> 00:37:46.880
...is there no one here man enough
to stay in the ring...

00:37:47.050 --> 00:37:51.760
...for three minutes
with this titan of testosterone?

00:37:54.340 --> 00:37:56.420
Who?

00:37:56.670 --> 00:37:58.550
I know who.

00:37:58.760 --> 00:38:03.540
The Flying Dutchman!

00:38:03.880 --> 00:38:05.340
Next.

00:38:06.170 --> 00:38:09.470
There's no featherweight
division here. Next.

00:38:09.630 --> 00:38:11.470
No, no. Sign me up.

00:38:11.880 --> 00:38:15.300
Okay. You understand the NYWL
is not responsible...

00:38:15.500 --> 00:38:19.680
...for any injury you may and probably
will sustain in said event?

00:38:19.880 --> 00:38:23.000
And you're participating
under your own free will?

00:38:23.170 --> 00:38:27.210
Down the hall to the ramp.
May God be with you. Next.

00:38:29.800 --> 00:38:32.040
Told you! Told you!

00:38:32.250 --> 00:38:34.040
Winner!

00:38:34.250 --> 00:38:35.460
Next victim!

00:38:37.340 --> 00:38:40.210
Are you ready for more?

00:38:41.330 --> 00:38:44.920
Bone Saw is ready!

00:38:47.340 --> 00:38:52.000
Will the next victim please
enter the arena at this time?

00:38:52.210 --> 00:38:56.920
If he can withstand just three minutes
in the cage with Bone Saw McGraw...

00:38:57.170 --> 00:39:01.540
...the sum of $3000 will be paid to...

00:39:02.420 --> 00:39:05.420
- What's your name, kid?
- The Human Spider.

00:39:06.000 --> 00:39:08.370
The Human Spider? That's it? That's the best you got?

00:39:08.540 --> 00:39:10.670
- Yeah.
- Oh, that sucks.

00:39:10.830 --> 00:39:15.340
The sum of $3000 will be paid to...

00:39:15.500 --> 00:39:18.750
...the terrifying, the deadly...

00:39:19.000 --> 00:39:22.210
...the amazing Spider-Man!

00:39:24.590 --> 00:39:27.200
- My name's, "The Human Spider."
- Get out there.

00:39:27.370 --> 00:39:30.420
- No, he got my name wrong.
- Get out there, you moron!

00:39:32.920 --> 00:39:35.450
Bone Saw will eat you up
and spit you out, little man.

00:39:35.700 --> 00:39:37.750
I hope you brought your mommy with you.

00:39:37.910 --> 00:39:42.170
- We'll break you!
- You'll need someone to cry to.

00:39:42.710 --> 00:39:47.830
I'm gonna rip all eight of your
feeble legs off one by one.

00:39:48.330 --> 00:39:50.370
Oh, my God!

00:39:50.580 --> 00:39:52.210
Oh, my legs!

00:39:52.380 --> 00:39:54.990
Oh, God. I can't feel my legs.

00:39:55.160 --> 00:39:57.160
Kill! Kill! Kill!

00:40:05.410 --> 00:40:06.910
Cage! Cage! Cage!

00:40:07.080 --> 00:40:08.290
Cage!

00:40:17.620 --> 00:40:19.080
Hello? Guys?

00:40:20.120 --> 00:40:25.080
Will the guards please lock
the cage doors at this time?

00:40:25.790 --> 00:40:30.080
This is some kind of mistake.
I didn't sign up for a cage match!

00:40:31.240 --> 00:40:33.740
Hey! Unlock the thing! Take the chain off!

00:40:33.950 --> 00:40:35.740
Hey, freak show!

00:40:35.950 --> 00:40:38.580
You're going nowhere.

00:40:38.750 --> 00:40:41.120
I got you for three minutes.

00:40:41.280 --> 00:40:43.580
Three minutes of playtime.

00:40:50.200 --> 00:40:53.660
- What are you doing up there?
- Staying away from you.

00:40:53.870 --> 00:40:57.910
That's a cute outfit.
Did your husband give it to you?

00:41:03.580 --> 00:41:05.120
Finish him off!

00:41:12.280 --> 00:41:13.830
Smash him!

00:41:20.990 --> 00:41:22.740
- Hit him!
- Harder!

00:41:24.740 --> 00:41:27.070
Kick his spider ass!

00:41:29.070 --> 00:41:30.240
Hit him!

00:41:43.660 --> 00:41:45.440
One, two, three!

00:41:45.650 --> 00:41:48.450
That's it! That's it!
Winner!

00:41:48.610 --> 00:41:53.700
Ladies and gentlemen, give it up
for the new champion, Spider-Man!

00:42:11.070 --> 00:42:12.740
Now get out of here.

00:42:14.360 --> 00:42:17.190
A hundred bucks? The ad said 3000.

00:42:17.400 --> 00:42:19.780
Well, check it again, webhead.

00:42:19.950 --> 00:42:23.820
It said three grand for three minutes.
You pinned him in two.

00:42:24.020 --> 00:42:27.400
For that, I give you 100.
You're lucky to get that.

00:42:27.570 --> 00:42:28.950
I need that money.

00:42:29.410 --> 00:42:32.480
I missed the part
where that's my problem.

00:42:40.570 --> 00:42:43.900
- Hey, what the hell...?
- Put the money in the bag.

00:42:45.730 --> 00:42:47.070
Hurry up!

00:42:53.400 --> 00:42:55.480
Hey! He stole the gate!

00:42:55.650 --> 00:42:57.610
Stop that guy!

00:42:57.900 --> 00:43:00.440
Stop him! He's got my money!

00:43:00.650 --> 00:43:01.900
Thanks.

00:43:03.150 --> 00:43:05.530
What's wrong with you?
You let him go!

00:43:05.690 --> 00:43:07.950
Cut him off and call the cops!

00:43:08.110 --> 00:43:12.150
You could've taken that guy apart.
Now he'll get away.

00:43:12.310 --> 00:43:15.690
I missed the part
where that's my problem.

00:43:34.070 --> 00:43:35.280
- You gotta get back.
- I can't see. What happened?

00:43:35.280 --> 00:43:36.980
- You gotta get back.
- I can't see. What happened?

00:43:38.230 --> 00:43:39.600
Old dude, man.

00:43:39.810 --> 00:43:43.980
Come on, folks. Keep moving, please.
Keep moving. Let's go!

00:43:44.150 --> 00:43:46.980
- What happened?
- Someone got hurt.

00:43:49.350 --> 00:43:52.570
- Excuse me. Excuse me. Excuse me.
- Stay back.

00:43:53.070 --> 00:43:54.900
- Stay back!
- That's my uncle!

00:43:57.060 --> 00:43:59.690
- What happened?
- Carjacker. He's been shot.

00:43:59.810 --> 00:44:03.360
We just called the paramedics.
They're on their way.

00:44:03.570 --> 00:44:04.930
Uncle Ben?

00:44:05.850 --> 00:44:07.350
Uncle Ben.

00:44:11.110 --> 00:44:12.440
Uncle Ben?

00:44:16.060 --> 00:44:17.560
Peter.

00:44:18.440 --> 00:44:20.230
I'm here, Uncle Ben.

00:44:25.850 --> 00:44:27.060
Peter.

00:44:49.020 --> 00:44:52.050
They got the shooter.
He's headed south on Fifth.

00:44:52.260 --> 00:44:56.980
We got three cars in pursuit.
All right, folks. Come on, move back.

00:47:33.920 --> 00:47:35.840
Get a unit to the rear!

00:47:38.880 --> 00:47:40.420
I got the back!

00:47:53.340 --> 00:47:54.670
Who's there?

00:48:20.920 --> 00:48:24.050
Don't hurt me. Give me a chance.
Give me a chance!

00:48:24.210 --> 00:48:28.710
What about my uncle?
Did you give him a chance? Did you?

00:48:28.880 --> 00:48:30.380
Answer me!

00:48:33.700 --> 00:48:35.040
Stop that guy!

00:48:40.500 --> 00:48:42.210
Thanks.

00:48:52.090 --> 00:48:53.200
See you.

00:49:14.870 --> 00:49:18.330
Freeze! We've got the place
completely surrounded.

00:50:00.780 --> 00:50:03.450
Oh, no. My God.

00:50:05.330 --> 00:50:09.030
Oh, no.
Oh, my God. No!

00:50:17.360 --> 00:50:20.330
- Good evening.
- General. Good to see you.

00:50:21.120 --> 00:50:24.000
Our exoskeleton's got
real firepower, general.

00:50:24.160 --> 00:50:29.570
Well, if it does what you say it can,
I'll sign that contract tomorrow.

00:50:30.280 --> 00:50:33.830
- He's clear! Go!
- You're confident about this test?

00:50:34.000 --> 00:50:36.280
Absolutely. Curtis is our top pilot.

00:50:37.030 --> 00:50:39.780
Now, what about
your commitment to OSCORP?

00:50:39.950 --> 00:50:43.860
Nothing would please me more
than to put Osborn out of business.

00:50:46.200 --> 00:50:49.240
Preflight complete. Mark.

00:50:53.360 --> 00:50:55.990
An unidentified object
is closing fast.

00:50:56.150 --> 00:50:57.240
What's that?

00:50:57.410 --> 00:50:58.910
Can you see anything?

00:50:59.370 --> 00:51:00.740
Oh, my God!

00:51:11.030 --> 00:51:13.860
- Say "chess."
- Chess!

00:51:14.360 --> 00:51:16.240
Peter!

00:51:16.450 --> 00:51:20.980
Darling, I'm so proud of you.
You looked so handsome up there.

00:51:21.150 --> 00:51:24.650
Dad got the place in New York,
so we're all set for fall.

00:51:24.820 --> 00:51:26.360
- Great!
- You made it.

00:51:29.120 --> 00:51:32.440
It's not the first time
I've been proven wrong.

00:51:33.860 --> 00:51:36.030
- Congratulations.
- Thanks, Dad.

00:51:36.450 --> 00:51:39.030
Peter, the science award.
That's terrific.

00:51:39.440 --> 00:51:40.730
Yeah.

00:51:43.690 --> 00:51:47.070
I know this has been
a difficult time for you...

00:51:47.240 --> 00:51:50.480
...but I want you to try
to enjoy this day.

00:51:50.690 --> 00:51:52.230
Commencement:

00:51:52.400 --> 00:51:56.530
The end of one thing,
the start of something new.

00:51:58.350 --> 00:52:02.030
I don't want to be with you anymore.
Here's your ring.

00:52:02.900 --> 00:52:04.780
You know what? Whatever.

00:52:05.320 --> 00:52:06.780
Your loss.

00:52:07.480 --> 00:52:11.020
You're like a brother to Harry.
That makes you family.

00:52:11.190 --> 00:52:15.030
And if you ever need anything,
give me a call.

00:52:28.900 --> 00:52:31.150
Can I fix you something?

00:52:31.320 --> 00:52:32.820
No, thanks.

00:53:17.520 --> 00:53:19.730
I missed him a lot today.

00:53:22.310 --> 00:53:23.810
I know.

00:53:25.560 --> 00:53:27.400
I miss him too.

00:53:29.150 --> 00:53:31.470
But he was there.

00:53:34.640 --> 00:53:39.860
I can't help thinking about
the last thing I said to him.

00:53:40.140 --> 00:53:45.060
He tried to tell me something important,
and I threw it in his face.

00:53:46.810 --> 00:53:48.900
You loved him...

00:53:50.560 --> 00:53:52.810
...and he loved you.

00:53:53.680 --> 00:53:57.350
He never doubted
the man you'd grow into.

00:53:57.520 --> 00:54:00.970
How you were meant for great things.

00:54:01.510 --> 00:54:03.850
You won't disappoint him.

00:54:37.340 --> 00:54:41.510
With great power
comes great responsibility.

00:54:41.680 --> 00:54:44.880
Remember that, Pete. Remember that.

00:54:54.880 --> 00:54:56.130
Hurry up!

00:55:08.510 --> 00:55:12.270
He's not a man. My brother saw him
build a nest in Lincoln Center.

00:55:12.430 --> 00:55:15.630
I think he's human, a man.
Could be a woman.

00:55:19.720 --> 00:55:22.460
Bobby. Get a load of this!

00:55:25.630 --> 00:55:29.890
He throws up his hands,
ropes come out, and he climbs up them.

00:55:30.180 --> 00:55:34.300
I see the web, his signature,
and I know Spider-Man was here.

00:55:34.470 --> 00:55:37.090
The guy protects us,
protects the people.

00:55:37.260 --> 00:55:40.010
Some kind of freakyloo or something.

00:55:40.180 --> 00:55:42.210
He stinks and I don't like him.

00:55:42.920 --> 00:55:44.510
Don't move, lady!

00:55:52.590 --> 00:55:55.340
Guy with eight hands. Sounds hot.

00:55:55.550 --> 00:55:57.680
Those tights and that tight little...

00:55:57.840 --> 00:56:01.170
Dresses like a spider
He looks like a bug

00:56:01.380 --> 00:56:05.130
But we should all just give him
One big hug

00:56:05.340 --> 00:56:09.920
Look out
Here comes the Spider-Man

00:56:13.590 --> 00:56:17.340
"Who is Spider-Man?"
He's a criminal, that's who he is.

00:56:17.510 --> 00:56:19.630
A vigilante, a public menace.
Why's he on my front page?

00:56:19.630 --> 00:56:20.500
A vigilante, a public menace.
Why's he on my front page?

00:56:20.500 --> 00:56:21.500
A vigilante, a public menace.
Why's he on my front page?

00:56:21.500 --> 00:56:22.010
Mr. Jameson, your wife needs...

00:56:22.010 --> 00:56:23.010
Mr. Jameson, your wife needs...

00:56:24.010 --> 00:56:24.840
- There's a page six problem.
- We have a page one problem.

00:56:24.840 --> 00:56:27.170
- There's a page six problem.
- We have a page one problem.

00:56:27.330 --> 00:56:28.880
- Well?
- He's news.

00:56:29.090 --> 00:56:31.590
- The clients can't wait.
- They're about to.

00:56:31.760 --> 00:56:35.760
- He pulled six people off a subway.
- From a wreck he probably caused.

00:56:35.930 --> 00:56:40.090
Something goes wrong and he's there.
Look! He's fleeing the scene.

00:56:40.250 --> 00:56:44.220
He's probably going to save
somebody else. He's a hero!

00:56:44.380 --> 00:56:47.170
Then why the mask?
What's he got to hide?

00:56:47.330 --> 00:56:50.380
She needs to know
if you want chintz or chenille.

00:56:50.550 --> 00:56:53.010
- Whichever's cheaper.
- It's like this:

00:56:53.170 --> 00:56:57.000
We double- booked page six.
Macy's and Conway's both have...

00:56:57.170 --> 00:57:00.340
- We sold out four printings.
- Sold out?

00:57:00.500 --> 00:57:01.710
Every copy.

00:57:02.510 --> 00:57:06.080
Tomorrow, Spider-Man, page one.
Move Conway to page seven.

00:57:06.250 --> 00:57:09.170
- That's a problem.
- Then make it page eight.

00:57:09.340 --> 00:57:11.000
- That can't be done.
- Get out!

00:57:11.170 --> 00:57:16.040
We can't get a decent picture. Eddie's
on it, but we can barely see him.

00:57:16.210 --> 00:57:18.340
Aw, what is he, shy?

00:57:18.500 --> 00:57:22.510
If we can get Julia Roberts
in a thong, we can get this weirdo.

00:57:22.660 --> 00:57:26.080
On the front page:
"Cash for a Spider-Man picture."

00:57:26.250 --> 00:57:29.710
He doesn't want to be famous?
I'll make him infamous!

00:57:42.160 --> 00:57:43.580
Buzz off.

00:57:44.290 --> 00:57:47.250
- M.J., it's me, Peter.
- Hi!

00:57:48.960 --> 00:57:53.830
- What are you doing around here?
- Begging for a job. How about you?

00:57:54.330 --> 00:57:58.040
- I'm headed to an audition.
- An audition? So you're acting?

00:57:58.210 --> 00:57:59.250
Yeah.

00:57:59.460 --> 00:58:03.330
I work steady.
In fact, I just got off a job.

00:58:03.500 --> 00:58:04.660
That's great.

00:58:05.250 --> 00:58:08.460
- You're doing it. Living your dream.
- Glamour girl!

00:58:08.630 --> 00:58:10.240
Your drawer was short $6!

00:58:10.410 --> 00:58:13.040
Next time, I'll take it
from your check.

00:58:14.120 --> 00:58:17.920
Excuse me, Miss Watson?
I'm talking to you! Hey!

00:58:18.130 --> 00:58:20.410
Yes, Enrique! Okay? I get you.

00:58:20.580 --> 00:58:24.710
It better not happen no more.
Don't roll your eyes at me.

00:58:31.660 --> 00:58:33.370
Some dream, huh?

00:58:34.250 --> 00:58:36.880
It's nothing to be
embarrassed about.

00:58:37.030 --> 00:58:39.830
- Don't tell Harry.
- Don't tell Harry?

00:58:40.240 --> 00:58:44.830
Don't you guys live together?
We're going out. Didn't he tell you?

00:58:45.250 --> 00:58:46.820
Oh, yeah. Right.

00:58:47.070 --> 00:58:50.160
I think he'd hate the idea
of my waiting tables.

00:58:50.330 --> 00:58:54.750
- He'd think it was low or something.
- It's not low. You have a job.

00:58:55.080 --> 00:58:59.410
You know, Harry doesn't live on
a little place I like to call Earth.

00:59:00.910 --> 00:59:02.830
No, I guess not.

00:59:07.820 --> 00:59:09.410
Thanks, Pete.

00:59:10.830 --> 00:59:12.750
We should catch up sometime.

00:59:16.950 --> 00:59:19.490
Let's get some lunch some evening.

00:59:20.740 --> 00:59:25.240
I'll come by and have some of your
Moondance coffee some day.

00:59:25.450 --> 00:59:28.160
- And I won't tell Harry.
- Don't tell Harry.

00:59:28.330 --> 00:59:29.580
I won't.

00:59:31.750 --> 00:59:33.490
I won't tell Harry.

00:59:44.780 --> 00:59:47.240
Timing's perfect. Hey.

00:59:47.450 --> 00:59:50.740
Five new contracts. It'll be great.

00:59:52.860 --> 00:59:55.570
Norman's making his weekly inspection.

00:59:56.370 --> 00:59:58.620
Spent half of it on the phone.

00:59:59.200 --> 01:00:03.900
Look, man, I'm glad you're here.
I need your help. I'm really lost here.

01:00:04.740 --> 01:00:06.030
Are you all right?

01:00:07.370 --> 01:00:11.900
You look like you just got
second place in the science fair.

01:00:13.200 --> 01:00:16.160
I was late for work
and Dr. Connors fired me.

01:00:16.320 --> 01:00:17.870
You were late again?

01:00:18.490 --> 01:00:22.440
I don't get it.
Where do you go all the time?

01:00:22.610 --> 01:00:23.860
Around.

01:00:24.030 --> 01:00:25.740
Peter Parker.

01:00:26.070 --> 01:00:28.570
- Maybe you'll tell me who she is.
- Who?

01:00:28.730 --> 01:00:31.820
- This mystery girl Harry's been dating.
- Dad.

01:00:32.190 --> 01:00:33.860
When do I get to meet her?

01:00:34.030 --> 01:00:37.320
Well, sorry.
Harry hasn't mentioned her.

01:00:40.190 --> 01:00:43.450
Pete, you're probably looking
for a job now, right?

01:00:43.650 --> 01:00:46.490
Dad, maybe you can help him out.

01:00:46.660 --> 01:00:50.980
- I appreciate it, but I'll be fine.
- I'll make a few calls.

01:00:51.150 --> 01:00:55.450
I couldn't accept it. I like to earn
what I get. I'll find work.

01:00:55.660 --> 01:00:57.270
I respect that.

01:00:57.980 --> 01:01:00.110
You want to make it on your own.

01:01:00.780 --> 01:01:02.110
That's great.

01:01:02.990 --> 01:01:05.320
What other skills do you have?

01:01:05.520 --> 01:01:07.650
I was thinking about photography.

01:01:10.610 --> 01:01:11.860
Hello.

01:01:13.780 --> 01:01:16.060
Let's go! Move it!

01:01:17.230 --> 01:01:18.900
Watch the street!

01:01:34.310 --> 01:01:35.690
Cheese!

01:01:44.600 --> 01:01:45.900
They're crap.

01:01:46.100 --> 01:01:49.070
Crap, crap. Megacrap.

01:01:49.270 --> 01:01:52.430
- I'll give you $200.
- That seems a little low.

01:01:52.640 --> 01:01:54.390
Take them somewhere else.

01:01:54.810 --> 01:01:58.900
- Your wife says the tile's out of stock.
- We'll put a rug there.

01:01:59.270 --> 01:02:01.230
Sit down. Give me that.

01:02:02.810 --> 01:02:05.350
Give you 300.
That's the standard fee.

01:02:05.520 --> 01:02:07.860
- Scrap page one. Run that.
- Headline?

01:02:08.150 --> 01:02:11.350
"Spider-Man, Hero or Menace?
Exclusive Photos."

01:02:11.520 --> 01:02:14.650
- Menace? He was protecting...
- You take the photos...

01:02:14.850 --> 01:02:17.520
...l'll make up the headlines. Okay?

01:02:17.690 --> 01:02:19.680
- Yes, sir.
- Goody.

01:02:20.140 --> 01:02:23.640
Give this to the girl up front.
She'll see you get paid.

01:02:24.100 --> 01:02:26.900
- I'd like a job, sir.
- No jobs. Freelance.

01:02:27.110 --> 01:02:28.730
Best thing for you.

01:02:28.940 --> 01:02:33.230
You bring me more shots of that clown,
maybe I'll buy them.

01:02:33.440 --> 01:02:36.400
But I never said you have a job. Meat.

01:02:36.560 --> 01:02:40.850
I'll send you a box of Christmas
meat. Bring me more photos.

01:02:42.430 --> 01:02:43.640
- Hi.
- Hi.

01:02:43.850 --> 01:02:47.270
Mr. Jameson told me
to give that to you.

01:02:48.350 --> 01:02:51.480
- Welcome to the Daily Bugle.
- Thank you.

01:02:52.020 --> 01:02:53.390
I'm Peter Parker.

01:02:55.900 --> 01:02:58.060
I'm a photographer.

01:02:58.850 --> 01:03:01.390
Yes. I can see that.

01:03:09.100 --> 01:03:10.930
As of today...

01:03:11.100 --> 01:03:15.100
...OSCORP Industries has surpassed
Quest Aerospace...

01:03:15.350 --> 01:03:19.770
...as the principal supplier
to the United States military.

01:03:19.930 --> 01:03:22.770
In short, ladies and gentlemen
of the board...

01:03:22.940 --> 01:03:26.090
...costs are down, revenues are up...

01:03:26.350 --> 01:03:29.180
...and our stock
has never been higher.

01:03:29.350 --> 01:03:33.770
Wonderful news, Norman.
That's why we're selling the company.

01:03:34.590 --> 01:03:35.840
What?

01:03:36.050 --> 01:03:41.180
Quest is recapitalizing in the wake
of the bombing. Expanding.

01:03:41.430 --> 01:03:44.180
They made a tender offer
we can't ignore.

01:03:44.340 --> 01:03:45.510
Why wasn't I told?

01:03:45.680 --> 01:03:49.770
They don't want a power struggle
with entrenched management.

01:03:50.060 --> 01:03:52.350
The deal is off if you come with it.

01:03:52.510 --> 01:03:55.930
The board expects your resignation
in 30 days.

01:03:56.140 --> 01:03:58.100
You can't do this to me.

01:04:01.270 --> 01:04:03.550
I started this company.

01:04:04.590 --> 01:04:07.010
You know how much I sacrificed?!

01:04:10.850 --> 01:04:16.300
- Oh, Max. Please.
- Norman, the board is unanimous.

01:04:16.850 --> 01:04:20.840
We're announcing the sale
after the World Unity Festival.

01:04:21.010 --> 01:04:22.510
I'm sorry.

01:04:23.510 --> 01:04:25.640
You're out, Norman.

01:04:35.510 --> 01:04:37.010
Am I?

01:04:40.800 --> 01:04:41.470
Welcome to OSCORP Industries
Unity Day Festival.

01:04:41.470 --> 01:04:43.970
Welcome to OSCORP Industries
Unity Day Festival.

01:04:43.970 --> 01:04:44.970
Let's hear it for Macy Gray.

01:04:44.970 --> 01:04:45.470
Let's hear it for Macy Gray.

01:04:45.470 --> 01:04:46.010
Let's hear it for Macy Gray.

01:04:46.010 --> 01:04:47.720
Let's hear it for Macy Gray.

01:05:24.090 --> 01:05:27.630
M.J., why didn't you wear
the black dress?

01:05:28.670 --> 01:05:32.340
Just, I wanted to impress my father.
He loves black.

01:05:32.510 --> 01:05:37.040
Well, maybe he'll be impressed
no matter what. You think I'm pretty.

01:05:37.590 --> 01:05:39.960
I think you're beautiful.

01:05:52.760 --> 01:05:56.000
I forgot my drink inside.

01:06:06.210 --> 01:06:08.340
- Oh, hi, Mr. Fargas.
- Oh, Harry.

01:06:09.420 --> 01:06:14.580
- Have you seen my father?
- Well, I'm not sure if he's coming.

01:06:26.590 --> 01:06:29.090
- What is that?
- Must be new this year.

01:06:33.960 --> 01:06:35.250
What is that?

01:06:35.420 --> 01:06:37.340
That's our glider!

01:06:47.710 --> 01:06:49.160
What the hell was that?

01:07:17.540 --> 01:07:18.950
Code three!

01:07:34.960 --> 01:07:37.120
- Oh, my God! Harry!
- M.J.!

01:07:43.080 --> 01:07:46.530
Harry! Help me! Harry!

01:07:52.500 --> 01:07:54.240
Out, am I?

01:07:58.790 --> 01:08:02.000
- Mary Jane!
- Harry!

01:08:03.990 --> 01:08:05.870
Hello, my dear.

01:08:06.870 --> 01:08:08.700
It's Spider-Man!

01:08:20.200 --> 01:08:22.150
- Come on. Move, kid.
- Billy!

01:08:25.660 --> 01:08:27.990
Somebody help him!

01:08:28.200 --> 01:08:30.250
No!

01:08:31.240 --> 01:08:32.780
Mommy!

01:08:34.780 --> 01:08:36.740
- Hold it!
- I surrender.

01:08:37.330 --> 01:08:39.830
- Oh, boy.
- Hold it right there!

01:08:45.620 --> 01:08:46.870
Lmpressive.

01:09:11.110 --> 01:09:14.570
- Mary Jane!
- Help! Someone please help me!

01:09:39.900 --> 01:09:40.950
Hold on!

01:09:42.570 --> 01:09:43.610
Watch out!

01:09:52.740 --> 01:09:56.520
We'll meet again, Spider-Man!

01:10:41.980 --> 01:10:44.650
Well, beats taking the subway.

01:10:44.860 --> 01:10:48.110
Don't mind us.
She just needs to use the elevator.

01:10:48.280 --> 01:10:49.400
Wait.

01:10:49.570 --> 01:10:50.810
Who are you?

01:10:50.980 --> 01:10:53.560
- You know who I am.
- I do?

01:10:53.770 --> 01:10:56.400
Your friendly neighborhood Spider-Man.

01:11:08.110 --> 01:11:11.980
Incredible?
What do you mean he's incredible?

01:11:13.150 --> 01:11:16.820
No. All right, wait.
Stay there. I'll come over.

01:11:17.480 --> 01:11:19.140
No, I'm gonna come...

01:11:19.480 --> 01:11:22.900
All right. Fine.
Will you call me in the morning?

01:11:23.100 --> 01:11:26.070
And we'll go and have breakfast and...

01:11:26.230 --> 01:11:28.520
...I want to buy you something.

01:11:28.680 --> 01:11:32.020
Because I want to.
It'll make you feel better.

01:11:33.060 --> 01:11:36.720
Okay. And what do you mean,
incredible?

01:11:39.560 --> 01:11:41.940
All right. I'm sorry. Sleep tight.

01:11:42.100 --> 01:11:43.850
Don't let the bedbugs...

01:11:49.520 --> 01:11:52.560
She's all right.
She's just a little rattled.

01:11:54.270 --> 01:11:57.890
Look, Pete, I should have
told you about us.

01:11:59.230 --> 01:12:01.890
But you should know
I'm crazy about her.

01:12:02.060 --> 01:12:05.100
It's just, you know,
you never made a move.

01:12:06.180 --> 01:12:07.680
You're right.

01:12:08.600 --> 01:12:10.100
I didn't.

01:12:14.100 --> 01:12:16.510
I'm gonna get some rest.

01:12:17.770 --> 01:12:20.020
I'm gonna stay up for a while.

01:12:21.100 --> 01:12:22.850
What was that thing?

01:12:23.430 --> 01:12:24.760
I don't know.

01:12:26.180 --> 01:12:29.560
Whatever it is,
somebody has to stop it.

01:12:45.430 --> 01:12:46.930
Somebody there?

01:12:46.930 --> 01:12:47.720
Somebody.

01:12:47.720 --> 01:12:49.390
Somebody.

01:12:50.730 --> 01:12:52.260
Who said that?

01:12:52.930 --> 01:12:56.260
Don't play the innocent with me.

01:12:58.720 --> 01:13:01.380
You've known all along.

01:13:05.390 --> 01:13:06.760
Where are you?

01:13:06.930 --> 01:13:10.970
Follow the cold shiver
running down your spine.

01:13:17.850 --> 01:13:19.670
I'm right here.

01:13:21.430 --> 01:13:23.430
I don't understand.

01:13:24.430 --> 01:13:27.600
Did you think it was coincidence?

01:13:27.850 --> 01:13:31.380
So many good things,
all happening for you.

01:13:31.550 --> 01:13:35.220
All for you. Norman.

01:13:37.760 --> 01:13:39.170
What do you want?

01:13:39.720 --> 01:13:41.760
To say what you won't.

01:13:42.050 --> 01:13:44.600
To do what you can't.

01:13:44.760 --> 01:13:49.340
To remove those in your way.

01:13:53.300 --> 01:13:55.260
The board members.

01:13:56.550 --> 01:13:57.920
You killed them.

01:13:58.090 --> 01:13:59.630
We killed them.

01:13:59.970 --> 01:14:01.010
We?

01:14:01.220 --> 01:14:02.760
Remember?

01:14:02.930 --> 01:14:05.590
Your little accident
in the laboratory.

01:14:07.460 --> 01:14:09.260
The performance enhancers.

01:14:09.420 --> 01:14:14.710
Bingo. Me!
Your greatest creation.

01:14:14.920 --> 01:14:18.710
Bringing you
what you've always wanted:

01:14:18.880 --> 01:14:21.760
Power beyond your wildest dreams.

01:14:21.930 --> 01:14:24.420
And it's only the beginning.

01:14:25.920 --> 01:14:30.260
There's only one who can stop us.

01:14:31.050 --> 01:14:34.420
Or imagine if he joined us.

01:14:39.220 --> 01:14:42.420
Spider-Man. And the Green Goblin.

01:14:42.670 --> 01:14:45.920
The Green Goblin. You like that?
Made it up myself.

01:14:46.090 --> 01:14:49.090
- These weirdos all got to have a name.
- Mr. Jameson...

01:14:49.260 --> 01:14:50.930
- Hoffman!
- Yeah?

01:14:52.130 --> 01:14:55.880
Copyright "Green Goblin."
I want a quarter every time it's said.

01:14:56.090 --> 01:14:58.380
How about "Green Meanie"?

01:14:58.550 --> 01:15:01.420
Spider-Man wasn't attacking.
That's slander.

01:15:01.580 --> 01:15:03.920
It is not. I resent that.

01:15:04.170 --> 01:15:06.920
Slander is spoken.
In print, it's libel.

01:15:07.090 --> 01:15:08.760
You don't trust anybody.

01:15:09.220 --> 01:15:10.960
I trust my barber.

01:15:11.790 --> 01:15:13.290
Are you his lawyer?

01:15:13.500 --> 01:15:18.260
Let him sue. Get rich like a normal
person. That's what made this country...

01:15:25.750 --> 01:15:28.870
Jameson, you slime.

01:15:29.080 --> 01:15:32.380
Who takes the pictures of Spider-Man?

01:15:32.580 --> 01:15:35.500
- I don't know. His stuff comes by mail.
- Liar!

01:15:35.670 --> 01:15:38.660
- I swear.
- He's the one who can bring me to him.

01:15:38.830 --> 01:15:41.750
- I don't know who he is.
- You are useless.

01:15:41.960 --> 01:15:44.210
Set him down, tough guy.

01:15:44.460 --> 01:15:49.040
- Speak of the devil.
- I knew you two were in this together!

01:15:49.250 --> 01:15:51.830
Kiddo, let Mom and Dad
talk for a minute.

01:15:52.040 --> 01:15:54.500
Sleep...

01:16:08.960 --> 01:16:12.960
Wake up, little spider. Wake up.

01:16:13.130 --> 01:16:17.540
No, you're not dead yet.

01:16:17.750 --> 01:16:19.910
Just paralyzed...

01:16:20.080 --> 01:16:22.040
...temporarily.

01:16:23.040 --> 01:16:26.120
You're an amazing creature,
Spider-Man.

01:16:26.330 --> 01:16:29.000
You and I are not so different.

01:16:29.710 --> 01:16:33.040
I'm not like you. You're a murderer.

01:16:33.250 --> 01:16:36.120
Well, to each his own.

01:16:36.290 --> 01:16:39.250
I chose my path,
you chose the way of the hero.

01:16:39.910 --> 01:16:44.530
And they found you amusing
for a while, the people of this city.

01:16:44.740 --> 01:16:48.000
But the one thing they love
more than a hero...

01:16:48.200 --> 01:16:51.790
...is to see a hero fail,
fall, die trying.

01:16:51.960 --> 01:16:56.490
In spite of everything you've done for
them, eventually, they will hate you.

01:16:56.700 --> 01:16:57.750
Why bother?

01:16:57.950 --> 01:17:02.660
- Because it's right.
- Here's the real truth.

01:17:03.070 --> 01:17:06.080
There are eight million people
in this city.

01:17:06.290 --> 01:17:10.580
And those teeming masses exist
for the sole purpose...

01:17:10.780 --> 01:17:14.740
...of lifting the few exceptional
people onto their shoulders.

01:17:14.910 --> 01:17:16.330
You, me...

01:17:16.910 --> 01:17:18.830
...we're exceptional.

01:17:19.080 --> 01:17:23.740
I could squash you like a bug
right now.

01:17:23.950 --> 01:17:27.620
But I'm offering you a choice.
Join me.

01:17:27.790 --> 01:17:31.360
Imagine what we could
accomplish together.

01:17:31.570 --> 01:17:34.330
What we could create.

01:17:34.910 --> 01:17:36.910
Or we could destroy.

01:17:37.080 --> 01:17:41.030
Cause the deaths of countless
innocents in selfish battle...

01:17:41.240 --> 01:17:46.120
...again and again and again until
we're both dead. Is that what you want?

01:17:48.110 --> 01:17:50.990
Think about it, hero.

01:18:02.950 --> 01:18:08.280
In spite of everything you've done for
them, eventually, they will hate you.

01:18:18.610 --> 01:18:20.070
It's me again.

01:18:20.450 --> 01:18:21.870
How was your audition?

01:18:22.070 --> 01:18:25.070
- How'd you know?
- The hot line. Your mom...

01:18:25.230 --> 01:18:27.190
...told my aunt, told me.

01:18:27.650 --> 01:18:28.990
So you just came by?

01:18:29.200 --> 01:18:32.820
I was in the neighborhood.
Needed to see a friendly face.

01:18:32.990 --> 01:18:37.570
I took two buses and a cab
to get in the neighborhood, but...

01:18:37.820 --> 01:18:39.320
So how'd it go?

01:18:41.490 --> 01:18:44.070
They said I needed acting lessons.

01:18:44.230 --> 01:18:47.990
A soap opera told me
I needed acting lessons.

01:18:48.150 --> 01:18:53.480
Let me buy you a cheeseburger.
The sky's the limit, up to $7.84.

01:18:54.820 --> 01:18:56.900
I'd like a cheeseburger.

01:18:57.360 --> 01:19:00.820
Oh, but I'm going out to dinner
with Harry.

01:19:01.240 --> 01:19:02.650
Come with us.

01:19:02.810 --> 01:19:05.570
No, thanks. How's it going with...?

01:19:07.490 --> 01:19:09.990
Never mind.
That's none of my business.

01:19:10.490 --> 01:19:11.980
It's not?

01:19:13.400 --> 01:19:15.070
Why so interested?

01:19:15.730 --> 01:19:17.240
I'm not.

01:19:17.490 --> 01:19:18.860
You're not?

01:19:20.490 --> 01:19:23.230
- Well, why would I be?
- I don't know.

01:19:23.480 --> 01:19:25.280
Why would you be?

01:19:27.150 --> 01:19:29.490
I, that's a...

01:19:29.700 --> 01:19:31.190
I don't know.

01:19:33.400 --> 01:19:36.230
Sorry you won't come with us.

01:19:38.700 --> 01:19:40.650
I'd better run, tiger.

01:19:49.350 --> 01:19:51.350
Hey, check it out, man.

01:19:51.520 --> 01:19:53.190
Come on, man.

01:19:56.740 --> 01:19:59.980
Hey, where you going, baby?
Come on!

01:20:17.850 --> 01:20:19.310
Get off me!

01:20:52.560 --> 01:20:54.060
Wait!

01:20:58.890 --> 01:21:01.270
You have a knack
for getting in trouble.

01:21:01.440 --> 01:21:05.810
You have a knack for saving my life.
I think I have a superhero stalker.

01:21:06.020 --> 01:21:07.890
I was in the neighborhood.

01:21:09.770 --> 01:21:12.390
You are amazing.

01:21:13.350 --> 01:21:16.060
Some people don't think so.

01:21:17.140 --> 01:21:20.150
- But you are.
- Nice to have a fan.

01:21:20.900 --> 01:21:24.100
Do I get to say thank you this time?

01:21:24.970 --> 01:21:26.470
Wait.

01:22:35.390 --> 01:22:37.510
Let me in! My baby's in there!

01:22:37.670 --> 01:22:39.800
- Let me go!
- The roof's collapsing!

01:22:39.970 --> 01:22:43.470
- Somebody save my baby!
- The roof's about to collapse!

01:22:43.680 --> 01:22:45.010
Look! Up there!

01:22:51.600 --> 01:22:53.430
Save my baby, please!

01:23:17.130 --> 01:23:18.260
No!

01:23:26.010 --> 01:23:30.010
- It's okay. Your baby's fine.
- Oh, my baby!

01:23:31.050 --> 01:23:33.960
God bless you, Spider-Man.
Bless you.

01:23:34.170 --> 01:23:35.920
Don't let him get away!

01:23:36.130 --> 01:23:39.380
Hold it! You're under arrest.
I'm taking you in.

01:23:39.550 --> 01:23:42.880
Oh, my God, there's somebody
still up there!

01:23:44.340 --> 01:23:45.670
I'm going.

01:23:47.340 --> 01:23:50.380
- I'll be here when you get back.
- Not coming back.

01:23:50.790 --> 01:23:51.920
Go! Go!

01:24:00.830 --> 01:24:02.540
Where are you?

01:24:04.590 --> 01:24:06.170
Where are you?

01:24:11.540 --> 01:24:13.920
I'm gonna get you out of here!

01:24:16.510 --> 01:24:18.000
It's okay.

01:24:25.050 --> 01:24:27.620
You're pathetically predictable.

01:24:27.790 --> 01:24:29.710
Like a moth to the flame.

01:24:30.580 --> 01:24:33.040
What about my generous proposal?

01:24:34.090 --> 01:24:36.910
Are you in or are you out?

01:24:37.120 --> 01:24:43.040
- It's you who's out. Out of your mind.
- Wrong answer.

01:24:43.460 --> 01:24:44.960
Oh, great.

01:25:23.580 --> 01:25:26.370
No one says no to me!

01:25:33.700 --> 01:25:37.120
- M.J., will you stop goofing around?
- Harry, relax.

01:25:39.620 --> 01:25:40.880
He's here.

01:25:41.660 --> 01:25:43.160
Are you ready?

01:25:45.000 --> 01:25:47.660
Aunt May. I'm sorry I'm late.

01:25:47.870 --> 01:25:50.950
Work was murder.
I picked up a fruitcake.

01:25:51.160 --> 01:25:54.580
Thank you, Mr. Osborn.
We're so glad you could come.

01:25:54.830 --> 01:25:57.540
Who is this lovely young lady?

01:25:57.710 --> 01:26:01.990
I'd like you to meet my father.
Dad, this is Mary Jane Watson.

01:26:02.200 --> 01:26:04.870
I've been looking forward
to meeting you.

01:26:05.080 --> 01:26:08.790
- Happy Thanksgiving, sir.
- Now, where is Peter?

01:26:08.960 --> 01:26:11.330
He'd better remember
that cranberry sauce.

01:26:17.080 --> 01:26:20.660
Oh, that's weird.
I didn't know he was here.

01:26:23.660 --> 01:26:25.160
Peter?

01:26:33.200 --> 01:26:34.910
Is that you?

01:26:40.370 --> 01:26:44.540
How strange. There's nobody here.

01:26:50.990 --> 01:26:55.450
- Bit of a slob, isn't he?
- All brilliant men are.

01:27:28.030 --> 01:27:30.660
- Hey, everyone.
- Oh, Peter!

01:27:30.820 --> 01:27:32.580
It's a jungle out there.

01:27:32.730 --> 01:27:36.650
Had to beat an old lady with a stick
to get these cranberries.

01:27:37.110 --> 01:27:39.950
Thank you.
Now then, everybody sit down...

01:27:40.120 --> 01:27:41.700
...and we can say grace.

01:27:45.240 --> 01:27:46.990
Here we go.

01:27:53.940 --> 01:27:56.280
- There we are.
- It looks delicious.

01:28:00.070 --> 01:28:02.360
Will you do the honors?

01:28:14.030 --> 01:28:17.280
Why, Peter, you're bleeding.

01:28:20.110 --> 01:28:25.440
I stepped off a curb and got clipped
by one of those bike messengers.

01:28:25.610 --> 01:28:27.150
Well, let me see.

01:28:27.360 --> 01:28:28.850
Oh, my goodness.

01:28:29.100 --> 01:28:31.520
- That looks awful.
- No, it's nothing.

01:28:31.690 --> 01:28:34.820
I'll get the first-aid kit.
Then we'll say grace.

01:28:35.030 --> 01:28:40.310
This is the boys' first Thanksgiving
here, and we'll do things properly.

01:28:41.270 --> 01:28:44.360
How did you say that happened?

01:28:44.780 --> 01:28:46.490
Bike messenger.

01:28:46.700 --> 01:28:48.650
Knocked me down.

01:28:54.030 --> 01:28:57.690
- If you'll excuse me, I've got to go.
- Why?

01:28:58.600 --> 01:29:01.980
Something has come to my attention.

01:29:02.190 --> 01:29:03.440
Are you all right?

01:29:03.650 --> 01:29:07.140
I'm fine, just fine.
Thank you, Mrs. Parker. Everyone.

01:29:07.770 --> 01:29:10.150
- Enjoy the fruitcake.
- Dad!

01:29:12.320 --> 01:29:16.100
I planned this so you'd meet M.J.,
and now you have to leave?

01:29:16.310 --> 01:29:17.980
I've got to go.

01:29:18.310 --> 01:29:22.440
- This girl is important to me.
- Harry, please. Look at her.

01:29:22.650 --> 01:29:26.600
Think she's sniffing around
because she likes your personality?

01:29:26.850 --> 01:29:29.860
- What are you saying?
- Your mother was beautiful.

01:29:30.020 --> 01:29:35.430
They're all beautiful until they're
snarling after your money like wolves.

01:29:35.640 --> 01:29:36.890
You're wrong, Dad.

01:29:37.440 --> 01:29:40.650
A word to the not-so-wise
about your girlfriend:

01:29:40.810 --> 01:29:44.680
Do what you need to with her,
then broom her fast.

01:29:55.060 --> 01:29:57.600
Thanks for sticking up for me, Harry.

01:29:57.810 --> 01:30:00.770
- You heard?
- Everyone heard that creep.

01:30:00.980 --> 01:30:04.850
That creep is my father.
With luck, I'll be half of what he is.

01:30:05.100 --> 01:30:07.440
Shut up about stuff
you don't understand!

01:30:07.600 --> 01:30:09.270
Harry Osborn!

01:30:10.360 --> 01:30:12.390
I'm sorry, Aunt May.

01:30:15.350 --> 01:30:18.690
Spider-Man is all but invincible.

01:30:18.850 --> 01:30:21.970
But Parker, we can destroy him.

01:30:22.180 --> 01:30:23.520
I can't.

01:30:23.680 --> 01:30:26.690
Betrayal must not be countenanced.

01:30:26.940 --> 01:30:29.180
Parker must be educated.

01:30:31.350 --> 01:30:32.640
What do I do?

01:30:32.850 --> 01:30:36.940
Instruct him in the matters
of loss and pain.

01:30:37.100 --> 01:30:40.140
Make him suffer.
Make him wish he were dead.

01:30:40.390 --> 01:30:41.680
Yes?

01:30:41.850 --> 01:30:43.770
And then grant his wish.

01:30:44.680 --> 01:30:45.980
But how?

01:30:46.190 --> 01:30:50.470
The cunning warrior attacks
neither body nor mind.

01:30:50.680 --> 01:30:51.850
Tell me how!

01:30:52.010 --> 01:30:54.180
The heart, Osborn.

01:30:54.430 --> 01:30:57.470
First, we attack his heart.

01:30:59.350 --> 01:31:02.850
Give us this day our daily bread,
and forgive us our trespasses...

01:31:03.060 --> 01:31:06.020
...as we forgive those
who trespass against us.

01:31:06.260 --> 01:31:10.100
Lead us not into temptation,
but deliver us...

01:31:17.840 --> 01:31:20.390
Deliver us!

01:31:20.600 --> 01:31:21.970
Finish it!

01:31:22.260 --> 01:31:26.180
- Finish it!
- From evil!

01:31:31.890 --> 01:31:34.050
Two milligrams IV.

01:31:35.840 --> 01:31:37.090
Get the BP.

01:31:37.510 --> 01:31:41.100
Aunt May. Is she gonna be okay?
What happened?

01:31:41.310 --> 01:31:42.640
You have to leave.

01:31:42.810 --> 01:31:44.510
- What happened?
- Those eyes!

01:31:44.670 --> 01:31:48.760
Those horrible yellow eyes!

01:31:53.590 --> 01:31:56.130
He knows who I am.

01:32:40.040 --> 01:32:41.630
I'm sorry.

01:32:45.340 --> 01:32:47.800
- Will she be okay?
- She'll be fine.

01:32:47.970 --> 01:32:50.630
She's been sleeping all day.

01:32:51.630 --> 01:32:54.380
- Thanks for coming.
- Of course.

01:32:58.540 --> 01:33:01.460
How are you?
You okay about the other night?

01:33:01.630 --> 01:33:05.340
Yeah, I'm fine. I just felt bad
about leaving Aunt May.

01:33:05.550 --> 01:33:08.500
- Have you talked to Harry?
- He called me.

01:33:08.960 --> 01:33:11.130
I haven't called him back.

01:33:13.210 --> 01:33:14.920
The fact is...

01:33:16.080 --> 01:33:18.920
...l'm in love with somebody else.
- You are?

01:33:19.080 --> 01:33:21.300
At least I think I am.

01:33:22.960 --> 01:33:26.000
- It's not the time to talk about it.
- No. Go on.

01:33:26.170 --> 01:33:29.420
Would I know his name, this guy?

01:33:29.630 --> 01:33:32.510
You'll think I'm a little girl
with a crush.

01:33:32.670 --> 01:33:34.050
Trust me.

01:33:34.300 --> 01:33:35.540
It's funny.

01:33:37.540 --> 01:33:41.500
He's saved my life twice,
and I've never even seen his face.

01:33:41.670 --> 01:33:45.040
- Oh. Him.
- You're laughing at me.

01:33:45.250 --> 01:33:48.210
No, I understand.
He is extremely cool.

01:33:48.420 --> 01:33:52.710
But do you think it's true,
all the terrible things they say?

01:33:52.880 --> 01:33:55.790
Not Spider-Man,
not a chance in the world.

01:33:56.000 --> 01:33:57.630
I know him a little bit.

01:33:57.830 --> 01:34:00.710
I'm sort of his unofficial
photographer.

01:34:00.920 --> 01:34:04.040
- Has he mentioned me?
- Yeah.

01:34:04.370 --> 01:34:05.830
What'd he say?

01:34:06.420 --> 01:34:07.750
I said...

01:34:08.830 --> 01:34:13.120
He asked me what I thought about you.

01:34:14.040 --> 01:34:16.080
And what did you say?

01:34:16.790 --> 01:34:20.880
I said, "Spider-Man."

01:34:21.200 --> 01:34:26.080
I said, "The great thing about M. J...

01:34:26.290 --> 01:34:27.830
...is...

01:34:28.750 --> 01:34:31.990
...when you look in her eyes...

01:34:34.540 --> 01:34:37.750
...and she's looking back in yours...

01:34:38.750 --> 01:34:41.740
...everything feels...

01:34:42.950 --> 01:34:44.790
...not quite normal.

01:34:46.040 --> 01:34:47.830
Because you feel...

01:34:48.380 --> 01:34:49.990
...stronger...

01:34:51.540 --> 01:34:55.160
...and weaker at the same time.

01:34:56.210 --> 01:34:58.320
You feel excited...

01:34:59.200 --> 01:35:01.240
...and at the same time...

01:35:01.870 --> 01:35:03.500
...terrified.

01:35:05.830 --> 01:35:10.120
The truth is, you don't know
what you feel...

01:35:11.540 --> 01:35:15.160
...except you know what kind of man
you want to be.

01:35:17.870 --> 01:35:19.740
It's as if you've...

01:35:20.370 --> 01:35:23.540
...reached the unreachable...

01:35:25.120 --> 01:35:27.820
...and you weren't ready for it."

01:35:31.290 --> 01:35:33.040
You said that?

01:35:33.830 --> 01:35:36.160
Well, something like that.

01:36:20.410 --> 01:36:21.900
Dad?

01:36:27.240 --> 01:36:29.330
Dad, is that you?

01:36:35.910 --> 01:36:37.410
What is it?

01:36:39.660 --> 01:36:44.650
You were right about M.J.
You're right about everything.

01:36:45.660 --> 01:36:48.370
She's in love with Peter.

01:36:48.660 --> 01:36:50.440
- Parker?
- Yeah.

01:36:50.610 --> 01:36:53.740
And how does he feel about her?

01:36:55.150 --> 01:36:57.700
He's loved her since the 4th grade.

01:36:58.660 --> 01:37:03.900
He pretends like he doesn't, but
there's no one Peter cares for more.

01:37:06.820 --> 01:37:08.560
I'm so sorry.

01:37:11.030 --> 01:37:14.490
I haven't always been there for you,
have I?

01:37:16.240 --> 01:37:19.440
You're busy. You're an important man.
I understand.

01:37:19.610 --> 01:37:21.440
That's no excuse.

01:37:22.440 --> 01:37:24.240
I'm proud of you.

01:37:24.780 --> 01:37:29.650
I've lost sight of that somewhere.
But I'll make it up to you.

01:37:29.820 --> 01:37:33.070
I'm going to rectify
certain inequities.

01:37:47.190 --> 01:37:48.980
Wake up, little spider.

01:37:49.150 --> 01:37:50.650
Wake up.

01:37:51.980 --> 01:37:53.570
Go home, dear.

01:37:53.780 --> 01:37:55.100
You look awful.

01:37:55.310 --> 01:37:57.610
- And you look beautiful.
- Thank you.

01:37:57.770 --> 01:38:01.110
- I don't like to leave you here.
- But I'm safe here.

01:38:01.280 --> 01:38:03.980
- Can I do anything for you?
- You do too much.

01:38:04.140 --> 01:38:09.690
College, a job, all this time with me.
You're not Superman, you know.

01:38:10.440 --> 01:38:12.190
A smile. Finally.

01:38:12.360 --> 01:38:16.690
Haven't seen one of those on your face
since Mary Jane was here.

01:38:16.850 --> 01:38:19.150
You were supposed to be asleep.

01:38:19.980 --> 01:38:24.730
You know, you were about 6 years old
when M.J.'s family moved in next door.

01:38:24.940 --> 01:38:28.940
When she got out of the car,
and you saw her for the first time...

01:38:29.150 --> 01:38:35.390
...you grabbed me and said,
"Aunt May, is that an angel?"

01:38:35.600 --> 01:38:39.150
- Gee, did I say that?
- You sure did.

01:38:41.810 --> 01:38:44.560
Well, Harry's in love with her.

01:38:44.770 --> 01:38:48.520
- She's still his girl.
- Well, isn't that up to her?

01:38:48.730 --> 01:38:53.310
- She doesn't really know who I am.
- Because you won't let her.

01:38:53.520 --> 01:38:56.650
You're so mysterious all the time.

01:38:56.900 --> 01:38:59.640
Tell me, would it be so dangerous...

01:38:59.850 --> 01:39:03.810
...to let Mary Jane know
how much you care?

01:39:04.270 --> 01:39:06.690
Everybody else knows.

01:39:09.600 --> 01:39:10.890
I'll be right back.

01:39:11.600 --> 01:39:12.890
But...

01:39:20.220 --> 01:39:22.230
Come on, pick up.

01:39:22.390 --> 01:39:25.690
- Hey M.J.
- Hi. Sing your song at the beep.

01:39:26.730 --> 01:39:28.760
M.J., it's Peter. You there?

01:39:29.060 --> 01:39:31.890
Hello? You there?

01:39:32.390 --> 01:39:36.890
I'm just calling to check up on you.
Will you call me when you get in?

01:39:37.050 --> 01:39:38.470
All right, well...

01:39:38.890 --> 01:39:39.930
Don't...

01:39:40.720 --> 01:39:42.930
Don't go up any dark alleys.

01:39:43.140 --> 01:39:44.640
Hello?

01:39:47.050 --> 01:39:50.770
Can Spider-Man come out to play?

01:39:50.970 --> 01:39:52.730
Where is she?

01:40:38.930 --> 01:40:40.600
- What is that?
- That's cool!

01:40:40.810 --> 01:40:45.430
The itsy-bitsy spider
Went up the water spout

01:40:45.590 --> 01:40:49.760
Down came the goblin
And took the spider out

01:41:06.550 --> 01:41:08.300
Goblin, what have you done?

01:41:50.710 --> 01:41:54.590
Spider-Man!
This is why only fools are heroes.

01:41:54.970 --> 01:41:56.630
Because you never know...

01:41:56.790 --> 01:42:01.550
...when some lunatic will come along
with a sadistic choice:

01:42:02.670 --> 01:42:05.290
Let die the woman you love...

01:42:09.590 --> 01:42:14.670
...or suffer the little children.

01:42:17.040 --> 01:42:19.550
- Spider-Man!
- Save us!

01:42:20.050 --> 01:42:22.340
Save us!

01:42:22.630 --> 01:42:25.210
Make your choice, Spider-Man...

01:42:25.420 --> 01:42:28.800
...and see how a hero is rewarded.

01:42:28.960 --> 01:42:31.050
Don't do it, Goblin!

01:42:31.210 --> 01:42:34.120
We are who we choose to be.

01:42:34.370 --> 01:42:37.130
- Now, choose!
- No!

01:43:05.790 --> 01:43:07.380
Everybody stay still!

01:43:16.880 --> 01:43:18.170
Ahoy up there!

01:43:18.340 --> 01:43:21.290
We're gonna bring the barge
right under you.

01:43:28.790 --> 01:43:32.910
- He's coming back!
- Listen. I need you to climb down.

01:43:33.080 --> 01:43:34.580
- I can't.
- Yes, you can!

01:43:39.660 --> 01:43:42.710
M.J., you can do it. You have to.

01:43:42.870 --> 01:43:44.460
Trust me.

01:43:45.960 --> 01:43:49.790
Hold on tight and go quickly.

01:43:54.120 --> 01:43:56.170
- Hurry!
- I can't. I can't do it.

01:43:56.380 --> 01:43:58.030
Hang on, Mary Jane!

01:44:26.450 --> 01:44:29.080
- He's not gonna make it.
- He's gonna make it!

01:44:38.950 --> 01:44:42.160
It's time to die.

01:44:49.160 --> 01:44:52.990
- I got something for you!
- We ought to kick your ass!

01:44:53.150 --> 01:44:56.570
Leave Spider-Man alone!
You'd pick on a guy saving kids?

01:44:57.240 --> 01:45:00.750
You mess with Spidey,
you mess with New York!

01:45:00.910 --> 01:45:04.450
You mess with one of us,
you mess with all of us!

01:45:16.950 --> 01:45:18.740
Spider-Man, watch out!

01:45:50.570 --> 01:45:54.820
Misery, misery, misery.
That's what you've chosen.

01:45:55.740 --> 01:45:58.360
I offered you friendship...

01:45:58.530 --> 01:46:00.400
...and you spat in my face.

01:46:51.440 --> 01:46:55.110
You've spun your last web, Spider-Man.

01:46:55.270 --> 01:46:58.610
Had you not been so selfish,
your girlfriend's death...

01:46:58.780 --> 01:47:00.440
...would have been quick.

01:47:00.610 --> 01:47:04.020
But now that you've really
pissed me off...

01:47:04.270 --> 01:47:09.150
...l'm gonna finish her
nice and slow.

01:47:13.730 --> 01:47:15.770
M.J. And I...

01:47:16.610 --> 01:47:19.900
...we're gonna have a hell of a time.

01:48:13.650 --> 01:48:15.190
Peter, stop!

01:48:15.360 --> 01:48:17.810
Stop! It's me.

01:48:26.760 --> 01:48:28.270
Mr. Osborn.

01:48:28.430 --> 01:48:29.980
Thank God for you.

01:48:30.180 --> 01:48:32.520
You killed those people
on that balcony.

01:48:32.690 --> 01:48:35.720
The Goblin killed!
I had nothing to do with it!

01:48:35.890 --> 01:48:37.640
Don't let him take me again.

01:48:37.810 --> 01:48:39.850
I beg you. Protect me.

01:48:40.020 --> 01:48:43.600
You tried to kill Aunt May.
You tried to kill Mary Jane.

01:48:43.770 --> 01:48:45.260
But not you.

01:48:45.930 --> 01:48:49.890
I tried to stop it.
But I couldn't stop it.

01:48:50.100 --> 01:48:52.190
I would never hurt you.

01:48:52.390 --> 01:48:54.300
I knew from the beginning...

01:48:54.510 --> 01:48:57.430
...if anything ever happened to me...

01:48:57.600 --> 01:48:59.720
...it was you I could count on.

01:48:59.890 --> 01:49:03.260
You, Peter Parker, would save me,
and so you have.

01:49:03.840 --> 01:49:05.680
Thank God for you.

01:49:06.680 --> 01:49:08.100
Give me your hand.

01:49:09.270 --> 01:49:12.680
Believe in me
as I believed in you.

01:49:14.090 --> 01:49:16.890
I've been like a father to you.

01:49:18.430 --> 01:49:20.100
Be a son to me now.

01:49:21.880 --> 01:49:23.760
I have a father.

01:49:24.510 --> 01:49:27.010
His name was Ben Parker.

01:49:28.890 --> 01:49:30.350
Godspeed, Spider-Man.

01:49:49.260 --> 01:49:50.760
Peter.

01:49:53.090 --> 01:49:54.930
Don't tell Harry.

01:50:26.590 --> 01:50:28.300
What have you done?

01:50:28.460 --> 01:50:30.050
What have you done?!

01:50:58.170 --> 01:51:00.220
I'm so sorry, Harry.

01:51:01.130 --> 01:51:04.250
I know what it's like
to lose a father.

01:51:06.420 --> 01:51:09.720
I didn't lose him.
He was stolen from me.

01:51:11.300 --> 01:51:13.580
One day Spider-Man will pay.

01:51:15.460 --> 01:51:18.590
I swear on my father's grave,
Spider-Man will pay.

01:51:23.580 --> 01:51:25.420
Thank God for you, Peter.

01:51:26.130 --> 01:51:28.590
You're the only family I have.

01:51:53.080 --> 01:51:55.380
No matter what I do...

01:51:55.540 --> 01:51:58.670
... no matter how hard I try...

01:51:59.250 --> 01:52:03.080
... the ones I love will always
be the ones who pay.

01:52:13.790 --> 01:52:16.130
You must miss him so much.

01:52:17.090 --> 01:52:20.120
It's been so hard without him.

01:52:23.040 --> 01:52:25.920
There's something
I've been wanting to tell you.

01:52:27.700 --> 01:52:29.500
When I was up there...

01:52:30.250 --> 01:52:33.040
...and I thought I was gonna die...

01:52:34.670 --> 01:52:38.500
...there was only one person
who I was thinking of.

01:52:39.790 --> 01:52:43.000
And it wasn't who I thought it'd be.

01:52:44.460 --> 01:52:46.870
It was you, Pete.

01:52:47.740 --> 01:52:49.620
I kept thinking:

01:52:50.040 --> 01:52:52.830
"I hope I make it through this...

01:52:54.290 --> 01:52:58.660
...so I can see Peter Parker's face
one more time."

01:53:00.040 --> 01:53:01.540
Really?

01:53:01.920 --> 01:53:07.700
There's only one man
who's always been there for me...

01:53:08.950 --> 01:53:10.910
...who makes me feel...

01:53:11.370 --> 01:53:15.080
...like I'm more than I ever
thought I could be.

01:53:17.200 --> 01:53:18.870
That I'm just...

01:53:19.540 --> 01:53:21.040
...me.

01:53:22.120 --> 01:53:24.030
And that's okay.

01:53:26.240 --> 01:53:27.700
The truth is...

01:53:29.830 --> 01:53:31.620
...I love you.

01:53:33.740 --> 01:53:35.660
I love you so much, Peter.

01:53:56.370 --> 01:54:01.110
All I wanted was to tell her
how much I loved her.

01:54:01.280 --> 01:54:03.200
I can't...

01:54:05.330 --> 01:54:06.870
You can't what?

01:54:08.000 --> 01:54:09.440
Tell you...

01:54:11.160 --> 01:54:15.490
...everything.
I mean, there's so much to tell.

01:54:16.580 --> 01:54:20.490
Yeah. There's so much to tell.

01:54:21.410 --> 01:54:23.370
I want you to know...

01:54:23.780 --> 01:54:26.450
...that I will always be there
for you.

01:54:26.660 --> 01:54:30.610
I will always be there
to take care of you.

01:54:31.610 --> 01:54:33.620
I promise you that.

01:54:36.910 --> 01:54:39.190
I will always be your friend.

01:54:42.110 --> 01:54:43.990
Only a friend...

01:54:44.870 --> 01:54:46.400
...Peter Parker?

01:54:48.570 --> 01:54:51.410
That's all I have to give.

01:55:17.730 --> 01:55:20.400
Whatever life holds in store for me...

01:55:20.570 --> 01:55:23.440
...I will never forget these words:

01:55:23.650 --> 01:55:28.690
"With great power
comes great responsibility. "

01:55:28.860 --> 01:55:31.110
This is my gift.

01:55:31.280 --> 01:55:33.400
My curse.

01:55:33.900 --> 01:55:35.820
Who am I?

01:55:36.190 --> 01:55:37.570
I'm Spider-Man.
